Need recall facts: Qin Shi Huang (嬴政, Ying Zheng), born 259 BC in Handan, Zhao state, son of Ying Zichu (秦异人/子楚), later King Zhuangxiang of Qin, and Lady Zhao (赵姬), a concubine/dancer from Zhao. His father was grandson of King Zhao of Qin? Actually Zichu was son of Prince Anguo (安国君, later King Xiaowen) and grandson of King Zhao of Qin. Ying Zheng became king at age 13 after father's death in 247 BC; Lü Buwei regent, then Lao Ai coup, etc. Family: mother Zhao Ji; father King Zhuangxiang; grandfather King Xiaowen (安国君); great-grandfather King Zhao of Qin; half-brothers? He had at least one younger brother, Ying Chengjiao (成蟜), who rebelled in 239 BC and was executed/killed? Also possibly brothers by mother with Lao Ai? The scandal: Zhao Ji had two sons with Lao Ai (嫪毐), allegedly; after Lao Ai's rebellion, the two infants were killed (one smashed?) and Zhao Ji imprisoned then later released. Ying Zheng had children: sons included 扶苏 (Fusu), 胡亥 (Huhai), 公子高 (Gao), 公子将闾 (Jianglu), 公子子婴? Actually Ziying was grandson? Need be careful. Qin Shi Huang had many sons; Fusu eldest, Huhai youngest/second son? Huhai was 18 at death in 210, born 229. Fusu born around 241? Qin Shi Huang had at least 23 sons? Records say he had many children; after death, Huhai and Zhao Gao forged edict. Sons Fusu and Meng Tian ordered suicide; Huhai became Qin Er Shi; later Ziying (son of Fusu? or grandson?) killed Zhao Gao. Need not list all.

Question: "历史中的秦始皇有甚么家人？他的童年过得开心吗？" Need answer: family members and childhood happiness. Need emphasize sources: Shiji etc, legends mixed. Childhood: born as hostage's son in enemy state Zhao; father Zichu was a Qin prince held hostage in Handan, low status, relied on Lü Buwei's scheme and Zhao Ji. Ying Zheng spent early childhood in Handan under threat; after Zichu became king (via Lü Buwei and Zhao), family returned to Qin around 251/250? Timeline: Zichu escaped Zhao with help of Lü Buwei and Zhao Ji? Actually Ying Zheng born 259; in 257 Qin army besieged Handan; Zichu escaped to Qin; Zhao Ji and Ying Zheng remained in Handan and were protected? Later after Zichu became king in 250/249, Zhao Ji and Ying Zheng returned to Qin. Ying Zheng's father died 247 when he was 13; mother Zhao Ji later involved with Lao Ai; scandal and coup when he was young (around 22? 238 BC he came of age, Lao Ai rebelled, executed; mother confined). So childhood likely not happy: political hostage, insecurity, loss of father young, mother's scandal, court intrigue, regency. But "happy" is subjective; no direct evidence of feelings. We can say from historical circumstances, unlikely carefree; he was raised amid danger and power struggles.

Need answer in Chinese. Mention names: 父亲秦庄襄王嬴子楚（异人），母亲赵姬；祖父秦孝文王（安国君），曾祖父秦昭襄王；弟弟成蟜；同母异父/传说中嫪毐所生二子（被处死）；儿子扶苏、胡亥、公子高、公子将闾等；女儿? Qin Shi Huang had daughters? Not well recorded; maybe 公主? Avoid specifics. Mention 吕不韦 not family but influential; 嫪毐 not family but mother's lover. Need clarify paternity rumors: Shiji records rumor that Ying Zheng was Lü Buwei's son, but this is likely slander/political rumor; mainstream historians treat as unreliable. Also Lao Ai claimed to be eunuch but actually had relations with Zhao Ji and had two sons; after exposure, Lao Ai executed, sons killed, Zhao Ji imprisoned.

